task: cluster-running-it
agent: opus-dataflow
started: 2026-09-11
branch: feature/cluster-running-it
worktree: ../okay-wt-cri1
spec: docs/modules/okay-cluster.md

why: the operator asked how to RUN distributed processing and the
  module's own doc could not answer it. It has an API table with
  `Cluster.run` and `WorkerMain` in it and a Tutorial from the P7 era
  — `Remote.listen`, `Cluster.distribute` — which is a different,
  older seam. Ten stages of engine and no page that says: start these
  processes, run this, here is what comes back.

what: a "Running it" section with the four roads and the commands,
  every one of them RUN BY HAND against real processes before being
  written down rather than recalled from the tests.

  It has to say the thing that is easy to get wrong and that I got
  wrong while checking: `Served.connect` dials EAGERLY, so a dead
  address throws before the run starts, and `Served.reconnecting`
  dials lazily and lets the coordinator place the failure. That is
  the difference between a demo that works and one that does not,
  and it is invisible from the API table.

predict: no code, and the risk is writing commands that are almost
  right. Every line goes through a terminal first; the classpath step
  is the one people will actually stumble on, so it gets a command
  rather than a description.
